The `_format` only strips when integer; for 7.5 it prints 6 decimals. I should trim trailing zeros. Better formatting: format then strip trailing zeros and dot.

```python
def _format(value, precision):
    if value.is_integer():
        return str(int(value))
    text = f"{value:.{precision}f}".rstrip("0").rstrip(".")
    return text
```

For 1/3 with precision 2 -> "0.33" already. For 7.5 -> "7.500000" -> strip -> "7.5". Good. Let me update.

